  "title": "",
  "body": "  The restriction map satisfies Its image is one-dimensional. The restrictions of Kähler classes form its positive ray, which has a unique primitive integral generator . This generator is an ample class.    Intersecting general divisors in high powers of gives All smooth fibres have the same homology class. Since , the polarized Fujiki formula implies that, for a positive constant , In each nonzero pairing of the copies of with the other classes, every copy of must be paired with one of the latter. Positivity of follows by taking all Kähler.  Choose a Kähler class on and let . One has . For a real class with , the mixed formula gives . If , it also gives . The Hodge–Riemann bilinear relations are negative definite on the real primitive classes, so . If , vanishing of the integral already gives that conclusion.  The classes in restrict to zero because is Lagrangian, and they are orthogonal to . The preceding argument therefore applies to every real class orthogonal to . Conversely, if , the mixed formula with in the remaining slots gives . This proves the kernel assertion and the rank-one image.  The kernel is defined over , so the image line is rational. Its intersection with has rank one. The positive generator is a positive real multiple of , hence is an integral Kähler class. It is therefore the first Chern class of an ample line bundle.   "
