  "body": "  The connection with parallel coframe makes affine special Kähler. In these affine coordinates the metric is the Hessian of The connection with parallel coframe is dual to with respect to .    The closed coordinate coframe gives flatness and zero torsion. The expression gives . Holomorphicity of implies Both right-hand sides are closed. In a parallel frame this is exactly .  Let . Since , one has The period relation gives and . Consequently, in the order , Substitution in the formula for gives exactly this matrix. It is positive definite. Its determinant is one, by taking the Schur complement of .  For a Hessian metric , define the dual connection by Its parallel coordinates are the gradient coordinates , since and the displayed identity makes these forms parallel. Here . This proves the assertion about the second connection.   "
