  "body": "  The metric is hyperkähler on . It descends to the quotient . In the complex structure of the holomorphic cotangent bundle, its holomorphic symplectic form is .    Identify a real covector with the holomorphic covector . The special Kähler condition makes the horizontal splitting compatible with this complex structure . In the splitting define where and is metric duality. Hermitian compatibility gives . Hence and , and all three are orthogonal for .  The forms defined by satisfy , so are closed. In affine Darboux coordinates , write a real fibre covector as . The remaining form is It is closed as well. The closedness criterion for an almost hyperkähler triple gives integrability and parallelness of ; this is the argument of .  Lattice sections are parallel for the connection induced on the cotangent bundle: their real parts are the defining parallel forms. Translation by any such section preserves the horizontal splitting, the metric and the three forms. The construction therefore descends to .   "
