  "body": " On a punctured disk , choose a branch of the logarithm and let Then and . A local primitive of is a prepotential. The lattice generated by defines a torus fibration over the punctured disk: after one positive circuit, becomes , so the lattice is preserved.  The base metric and the first affine monodromy are The second monodromy is . The affine connections are flat, but , so the Kähler metric is curved. The puncture is at finite radial distance because . The lattice and the semi-flat metric have singular behaviour there. Extending across that point requires a singular-fibre model.  "
