  "body": " Let be a smooth fiber bundle with compact fibers, and let be a compact smooth manifold. Suppose there is a smooth map over whose restriction to each fiber is an embedding. Fix a base point, write for its fiber, for the embedding, and for the cohomological monodromy. Then for every . If is unipotent, then .  Pullback along is a map from the local system to the constant local system . It commutes with transport around the circle, and transport in the target is the identity. Thus . This argument can also be seen by trivializing the bundle over an interval: the two endpoint embeddings differ by the bundle monodromy and are homotopic through the given parametrized embeddings.  Put . If is nilpotent, then The second factor is a finite polynomial in with constant term one. It is invertible and commutes with , proving equality of the two images.  "
