  "title": "(Engel–Mauri; OpenAI).",
  "body": " (Engel–Mauri; OpenAI)  Let be a nontrivial nef line bundle on a compact IHS manifold , with . Then is semiample. A globally generated positive power defines, after Stein factorization, a holomorphic Lagrangian fibration on .   Write as at the start of the chapter. The prescribed degeneration belongs to the marked component containing . Its smooth fiber therefore represents a point in that same component. Hyperkähler rotation from to is a path in its twistor sphere, so the rotated remains in the component.  At the original point , the class is of type , nef, and has positive pairing with the Kähler cone. At , it is of type and has the same positive sign by . Thus both endpoints lie in . By , its semiample locus is nonempty. Applying at the nef point shows that is semiample.  Choose with globally generated. Then is globally generated. The fibration assertion follows from : the numerical dimension of a nonzero nef isotropic class is , and the fibers of the resulting morphism are Lagrangian.   "
