  "title": "Notation",
  "body": " Notation   An IHS manifold, its underlying smooth manifold, and its dimension. A general Calabi–Yau degeneration has dimension ; the hyperkähler application has . See the conventions .  The primitive integral BBF bilinear form and the Fujiki constant in . We write .  The specified nef isotropic line bundle, its first Chern class, and the positive primitive integral generator of its ray; for an integer . See .  A Lagrangian fibration, its smooth-value locus, and its reduced discriminant. In the local geometry, is smooth; a normal global base is restricted to its smooth locus as specified. See .  The primitive integral polarization of a smooth fibre and its polarization type. This class is distinct from the fibration class , whose restriction to the fibre is zero. See . The subscript is omitted when the fibre is specified.  The fibre period lattice in the cotangent bundle, local special coordinates, and the symmetric period matrix with positive imaginary part. See and . The parameter in the ternary period construction below has a separate local meaning.  The relative translation group of , its dual , and the finite kernel of the primitive fibre polarization. The family is a -torsor. See .  The sheaf of vertical translations extending to the compactification, its first cohomology, and the twist determined by . See . The zero twisting class gives the original fibration and need not give a fibration with a section.  on a smooth fibre Local monodromy around a discriminant component and its logarithm after unipotent base change. The elliptic example in specifies both homology and dual cohomology conventions. This is monodromy of the fibres of .  Numerical dimension and Iitaka dimension, defined in . For nonzero nef isotropic , ; semiampleness gives .  A hyperkähler metric, a quaternionic triple, and . Thus , , and . See .  The normalized volume form and the phase of a special Lagrangian submanifold, measured by its positive calibration. See .  A special Lagrangian or holomorphic Lagrangian torus, an angular coordinate torus near a maximal crossing, and its Poincaré dual with a specified orientation. See and .  Monodromy of a degeneration of the whole IHS manifold on , its logarithm after unipotent base change, and the limiting weight filtration centered at . In degree two the prescribed degeneration has . See .  The polarization class, a rational ternary space of signature , and a basis with , , , and . These are local to the period construction in .  The normalized period . The real part is chosen irrational in the main proof; approaches the prescribed rational boundary point.  The parameter and the probability measure obtained by normalizing . See . A measure estimate uses this measure, whereas metric convergence requires a specified rescaling.  The analytification of the generic fiber over and its essential skeleton. Valuative independence and weak comparison are defined in and .  The positive locus in a fixed marked Teichmüller component on which is of type . Its nef and semiample loci are compared in .   "
